        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/modern-warfare-4-dmz-screen-2-crop.jpeg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/infinity-ward\">Infinity Ward</a> opened up early access to <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-dmz-early-access-no-pve\">Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 4's DMZ extraction mode overnight</a>, meaning anyone who has pre-ordered a copy can now play <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-parry-melee-best-moments\">the game's campaign</a> as well as DMZ. And while early reactions to DMZ are fairly positive, there's one issue in particular, which a number of players have experienced, that has the capability of ending a round as soon as it begins.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-dmz-spawn-runover\">Read more</a></p>",
