        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/blood-ravens-lore.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Right, let's get one important thing out of the way first: I've played a fair bit more of <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/warhammer-40000-dawn-of-war-4\">Dawn of War 4</a>'s main campaign, after <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/ive-played-warhammer-40k-dawn-of-war-4-and-it-feels-like-the-sequel-to-the-original-that-rts-fans-always-wanted\">my initial impressions of a single mission last year</a>, and I think it is <em>very good</em>. The action is as screen-filling as ever, the Orks are a delight, and the combat director, which sees individual combatants lock onto each other with bespoke animations when groups fight in melee, remains a genuine feat of RTS engineering. I'll have much more to say on that front soon, though I'd like a little more time with it first.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/dawn-of-war-4-blood-ravens-space-marine-origins-questions\">Read m",
